// The checked-in target graph, compiled in.
//
// **Generated at configure time from `mono.tools/architecture/expected_graph.json`,
// which is the file `just test-architecture` checks the build against.** Nothing
// here is edited: `mono.engine/control/CMakeLists.txt` reads that file and writes
// this one, and `CMAKE_CONFIGURE_DEPENDS` re-runs when it changes.
//
// **Compiled in rather than read from disk**, because a program answering this
// is a dedicated server or an editor started from wherever somebody happened to
// be standing. A tool that could only answer when the current directory was the
// repository would be a tool that fails exactly when a model most needs it, and
// the graph is a constant of the build rather than state of the run.

// **One literal per 16 KiB chunk.** MSVC refuses a single string literal over
// 65,535 bytes (C2026) and the graph grows toward that every time modules are
// added, so `mono.engine/control/CMakeLists.txt` splits the JSON by byte
// offset into adjacent raw string literals. Translation phase 6 concatenates
// them back into one string before the compiler ever sees it, byte for byte.
// The indexed delimiter stays under the standard's 16-character raw-delimiter
// cap and keeps one chunk's closer from matching another's content.

namespace engine::control {

	extern const char *const GRAPH_JSON;

	const char *const GRAPH_JSON =
@MONO_CONTROL_GRAPH_LITERALS@;
}
